e(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return True if the three\n    sides form a right-angled triangle, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Convert inputs to float to handle various numeric types and ensure consistency.\n    sides = sorted([float(a), float(b), float(c)])\n    x, y, z = sides[0], sides[1], sides[2]\n\n    # Sides must be positive.\n    if x <= 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # Check the triangle inequality: the sum of the lengths of any two sides\n    # of a triangle must be greater than the length of the third side.\n    # If x + y <= z, it cannot form a triangle.\n    if x + y <= z:\n        return False\n\n    # Check Pythagorean theorem using a tolerance for floating-point comparison.\n    # The longest side squared should be approximately equal to the sum of the squares of the other two sides.\n    # Using default tolerance from design context (1e-9) and rel_tol=0.0 as specified.\n    return math.isclose(x*x + y*y, z*z, rel_tol=0.0, abs_tol=1e-9)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}, {"task_id": "HumanEval/157", "solution": "def right_angle_triangle(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return True if the three\n    sides form a right-angled triangle, False otherwise.\n    A right-angled triangle is a triangle in which one angle is right angle or \n    90 degree.\n    \"\"\"\n    epsilon = 1e-9  # Tolerance for floating-point comparisons, as per design.\n\n    # Sort the sides to identify the potential hypotenuse (z) as the largest side.\n    sides = sorted([a, b, c])\n    x, y, z = sides[0], sides[1], sides[2]\n\n    # Check the triangle inequality: the sum of any two sides must be strictly greater than the third.\n    # If this condition is not met, it's not a valid triangle (including degenerate cases).\n    if not ((x + y) > z):\n        return False\n\n    # Apply the Pythagorean theorem: a^2